ne and China and other things.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: John Brennan, who is director of CIA under President Barack Obama, it`s always great to hear your thoughts on this. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 BRENNAN: Thanks, Chris.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Still ahead, the Trump family development igniting international backlash. People in the streets, that`s next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [20:36:58]\par \par \uc2 HAYES: I want to take you for a minute to a truly beautiful place, place I just learned about, in fact, it`s called Sazan. It`s a small island off the coast of Albania, covering about two square miles. On a nice day, you can even see it from the heel in Italy`s boot. And it is a sight: clear blue water, sandy beaches, rocky cliffs, rain forests, even a few majestic peaks, and 40 miles of hiking trails. The island`s location and climate make it quite unique. It explodes with a diversity of animal and plant life that you simply cannot find anywhere else. It`s almost untouched by people, and to keep it that way, Albania designated the beaches and the waters around Sazan as a maritime national park in 2010.\par \par \uc2 The mainland coast across from the island is one of the last wild river deltas in all of Europe. It`s also protected under law.\par \par \uc2 Now, a small number of mostly local tourists travel out to see the flamingos and the pelicans, their loggerhead turtles and monk seals, and dozens more endangered species, according to local naturalists.\par \par \uc2 Back in 2021, Sazan Island was discovered by a pair of seafaring explorers who would ultimately claim it as their own.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 IVANKA TRUMP, DONALD TRUMP`S DAUGHTER: I`m working on an incredible project with my husband in the Mediterranean. It`s massive in scale.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SENRA, FOUNDERS PODCAST HOST: I think that`s an understatement. Can you explain?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: It is.\par \par \uc2 SENRA: There`s no power on this island