xtraordinary.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Here is that extraordinary vision in action. According to videos posted by local activists, bulldozers, dump trucks, and razor wire already ripping up the mainline coastline.\par \par \uc2 And it is government-protected land. Again, it is against the law to develop there, unless the Albanian government changed its mind for some reason.\par \par \uc2 Well, just a few weeks after Donald Trump won the 2024 election, the government of Albania overrode its own environmental laws and greenlit the Kushners to develop the coastline and a chunk of Sazan Island with hotels, apartments, vias, and a marina.\par \par \uc2 Kushner`s firm has said the plan is to build a five-star eco-resort community on the island and to be quote, I quote here, "Faithful and considerate of the environment."\par \par \uc2 The whole project is through Kushner`s private equity company, which is, of course, flush with billions of dollars from Saudi Arabia and other Middle East sovereign wealth funds, money that was invested with him after he left the White House first time.\par \par \uc2 Remember, he was -- those are the ones he was soliciting while also advising the president on Middle East diplomacy.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Albania`s prime minister defended the deal in Trump-like terms.\par \par \uc2 EDI RAMA, ALBANIAN PRIME MINISTER: There is not such a thing like Trump family island. There is not such a thing like the family of the American president taking over protected areas where flamingos will be -- will be killed by them. The project is not yet there. The environmental impact is being worked, you understand. And let me finish.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, go ahead.\par \par \uc2 RAMA: Let me finish. What is this? What`s wrong with you.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I said go ahead.\par \par \uc2 RAMA: Let me finish.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: There is no need to be disrespectful. I`m asking you to go