e-over): And the Trump family moves in for a potential payday.\par \par \uc2 ERIC TRUM, SON OF PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP: There`s rampant corruption and it sucks and it shouldn`t happen and it`s disgusting.\par \par \uc2 HAYES (voice-over): Tonight, the big winners of Trump`s trip to China and new reporting that Trump`s \uc2 IRS\uc2  lawsuit could turn into a slush fund for Trump`s allies.\par \par \uc2 Plus, today`s fascinating victory for reproductive rights at the Supreme Court. All that and the new reporting on Kash Patel`s VIP snorkeling adventure in Pearl Harbor.\par \par \uc2 KASH PATEL, DIRECTOR, \uc2 FBI\uc2 : I`m the first one in, I`m the last one out. I`ve never been intoxicated on the job.\par \par \uc2 HAYES (voice-over): When ALL IN starts right now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HAYES (on camera): Good evening from New York. I`m Chris Hayes. Is there a single person on earth who believes, really believes that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in China to represent the public interest, to help ordinary Americans put America in the best possible position?\par \par \uc2 It`s what state visits like these are supposed to be about. But with Trump, it feels like a lot of money grubbing private interest. Let`s just start with who he`s traveling with. His retinue. Some of the richest and most powerful people on Earth. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , \uc2 Jensen Huang\uc2  of \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Cook\uc2  of \uc2 Apple\uc2 , \uc2 Dina Powell\uc2  of Meta, about a dozen others from companies like \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  and \uc2 Boeing\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What do you think their agenda is during this trip? Do you think they`re focused on what`s best for like the American middle class, the working class, or are they focused on what`s best for them, for their shareholders and their boards? Well, we know the answer.\par \par \uc2 Reuters is reporting that, "A critical precondition for companies to join the trip was having a tangible ask that promised a concrete outcome 