ike dominating the news for a week. But again, just all so used to headlines like that. It`s baked in. It`s baked in. We know it. Trump and the family and the people around him will take every single opportunity to enrich themselves regardless of the optics. The corruption has become so common place. It`s not news.\par \par \uc2 Here`s another example. Again, these are jut from today. I`m just doing today`s news. So, back in 2024, the Biden DOJ indicted India`s richest man, Gautam Adani, for corruption and fraud. Adani then hired, wait for it, ready, one of Trump`s personal lawyers as his representation.\par \par \uc2 Now, I could stop there and be like, guess how this ends up, ladies and gentlemen? Well, as a New York Times reports, Trump`s lawyer got Adani a meeting with the DOJ last month where he made the government an offer. He went through the case and all the reasons they shouldn`t prosecute and why they had a strong defense. But then there`s a slide that said if they drop the case, Adani would invest $10 billion in the U.S. economy and create 15,000 jobs.\par \par \uc2 First of all, do we think that`s really going to happen? But also, what the hell, dude? That has nothing to do with a criminal case. Well, today the Times reported that lo and behold, the DOJ will drop the charges. Sure, it feels like they proffered a bribe. I mean, again, maybe not to Trump`s pockets directly, but it gives him achievement to tout, right? That`s the whole point. Which brings us today, and again, we are just doing today`s news as the president is in China, just today`s news, OK. That brings us to the piece de resistance. What I like to think of as the Sistine Chapel of Trump corruption, what you might call the great heist.\par \par \uc2 Yes, it`s the story we covered last night in which Donald Trump is trying to shake down his own government, the one that he controls for 10 billion with a B Donald Trump dollars. OK. He`s suing the IRS for his tax returns leaking in which by the