ned.\par \par \uc2 This is about one-tenth of the size of the audience that watches this program. No presidential candidate has ever banned more books than \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . And he was joined in his announcement by the owner of \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , who claims to be a free speech advocate.\par \par \uc2 The latest victim of the DeSantis book banning laws in Florida, is the youngest poet ever to speak at a presidential inauguration.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 AMANDA GORMAN, POET: Mister President, Dr. Biden, Madam Vice President, Mr. Emhoff, Americans and the world. When day comes we ask ourselves, where can we find light in this never-ending shade. The loss we carry, a sea we must wade, we`ve braved the belly of the beast.\par \par \uc2 We`ve learned that quiet isn`t always peace in the norms and notions of what just is isn`t always just is.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 O`DONNELL: That poem was heard that day by children of all ages, around the world. Amanda Gorman was 22 years old, and a recent graduate of Harvard College on inauguration day. She had become the national youth poet laureate at 17 years old. She`s now 25 years old.\par \par \uc2 There may be no more inspiring poet for young American students in our history than Amanda Gorman. But thanks to \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ` censorship law, a single parent was able to have Amanda Gorman`s poem removed from an elementary school in Miami-Dade County -- one parent. That one parent insists that Amanda Gorman`s poem has, quote, "indirect hate messages". That is a lie.\par \par \uc2 There is not a single line in the poem that isn`t positive and isn`t appropriate for children of all ages, including pre verbal infants.\par \par \uc2 The poem does say that Amanda Gorman is, quote, "descended from slaves and raised by a single mother".\par \par \uc2 As of tonight, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is much better at book banning than he is at running for president. In his public discussion with 