pit of the Oval Office, denied that anything ever happened at \uc2 Bergdorf Goodman\uc2  and basically accused Jean of being a liar.\par \par \uc2 And she got $3 million for the second libel that occurred in 2022 when he was dumb enough to repeat that first libel and in this time he wasn`t president, so he didn`t have this legal argument -- that`s why the first case went off on a wild goose chase in the appellate courts, but now it`s come back. He`s now -- that case already had more damages potentially than the case that she already won, than the $3 million she already won because he was president at the time. It was the first -- the very, very first libel that he made on Jean Carroll.\par \par \uc2 And now, the fact that he has repeated the libel after being found to have sexually abused her and libeled her is really, really -- it`s outrageous and it`s supportive of punitive damages. This verdict could be greater than the $5 million that she got in the first case. Oh, frankly, I hope it is because I think at some point, he`s got to stop lying about this and stop libeling her. I mean, how many times do we have to go through this?\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Well, this is interesting. Trump`s attorney`s response is Ms. Carroll`s 11th-hour attempt to amend her complaint exposes the true motivation behind her numerous lawsuits. And it`s like, yes, the true motivation is to get him to stop defaming her. I think it`s pretty clear. I`m like, yes.\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: (INAUDIBLE).\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Yes. Let`s talk about -- let`s talk about the Jack Smith reporting in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 . I have to say, I was like, wait, what? They`re looking at his --\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: I mean, yes.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: -- business records in 2017, what do you make of that?\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: I -- well, look, I mean, I don`t think he needed a financial incentive to do what he did. I think his --\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Agreed.\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: -- his insane narcissism and his