ar \par \uc2 HAYES: Trump`s confidence aside from where I`m standing, securing Pence`s cooperation sure seems like a sign that Smith`s investigation is approaching its end game. In turn, this raises a question. And it`s not a sort of substantive question, it`s not a question about the sort of what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is accused of doing, it`s just a purely political question for a second if you`ll indulge me.\par \par \uc2 Here`s the question. Do Republicans really want to back Trump a third time? I mean, that clip you saw, right? He`s in New Hampshire today campaigning, gearing up for his third consecutive presidential campaign. He`s in the process over the last month, I would say, of consolidating the Republican field behind him. His lead has widened over his closest rival \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . And in fact, a new piece in Politico today outlines how many Republicans are effectively resigning themselves to the fact that that man, the one who attempted to overthrow an election, will be the Republican nominee.\par \par \uc2 One Republican strategist saying, "We`re just going to have to go into the basement, ride out the tornado, and come back up when it`s over to rebuild the neighborhood." That`s an amazing metaphor. Like, good luck everyone else who might be in the path of their tornado, we`ll be cowering in the basement while all of your stuff gets destroyed. But I don`t think they can escape the destruction. Trump is currently under indictment for the hush money payments he made to adult film actress Stormy Daniels. Again, a first in American history.\par \par \uc2 Now, on top of that, the woman who has accused Trump of raping her, E. Jean Carroll, has been under oath for two days taking a stand against him in civil court testifying about what she says was his rape of her. Fulton County District Attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  is signaling another possible indictment of Trump could come this summer, with a memo she said to law enforcement. And now Trump`s own 