rom today.\par \par \uc2 The country appears to be on a kind of precipice, amidst yet another round of violence between Israelis and Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 To sort through this, I talked to Edo Konrad, the editor-in-chief of an English language online publication about Israel and Palestine, called +972 Magazine on my podcast, why is this happening? I asked him about his perspective on these protests as a member of the Israeli left.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EDO KONRAD, EDITOR-IN-CHIEF, +972 MAGAZINE: The Israeli public has woken up to what it means to have far right -- the far right run its country. And they`ve started to wake up to realize, OK, these people have been kind of waiting in the wings, building their power for decades.\par \par \uc2 If I can make an analogy to the -- to the United States and to the conservatives into the Republican Party, the attempt to enshrine minoritarian rule, right, like this attempt to like in the United States to take over state legislatures and to ensure that next time there`s an election to make sure that the Republicans are able to basically stop the count or reverse the count or, you know, make sure that that a Democratic candidate is not elected.\par \par \uc2 It`s different in the Israeli system. But the logic is the same, to ensure far-right minoritarian rule forever in the court, I think is one of the things that really stops the far-right from achieving that goal.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HAYES: You can scan the Q.R. code on your screen right now to listen that full episode and find Why Is This Happening wherever you get your podcasts.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [20:52:21]\par \par \uc2 HAYES: One week ago, a Texas man named Daniel Perry was convicted of murder. He hasn`t been sentenced yet. But Texas Governor Greg Abbott already says he wants to pardon him.\par \par \uc2 And to be clear, this is not a case of someone being wrongfully convicted. No one is d