uc2 DOVER: Hey, guys! So, I know it`s been a really long time and I really don`t even know where to begin, but I guess I could start with I`m alive.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 VELSHI: Brandy Zadrozny has the full story of the wild conspiracy theory around that nurse you just heard from and the lessons on stamping out a lie in 2023. That`s just a head.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [20:45:00]\par \par \uc2 VELSHI: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is coming off a week where he was arraigned on 34 felonies in New York by trying to limit potentially explosive testimony against him in a different criminal investigation. The ex-President filed an appeal in a D.C. Federal Court today to block or narrow the scope of testimony from his former vice president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  , about Trump`s efforts to overturn the 2020 election. Pence would seem to have a lot to tell the grand jury in that probe because in the weeks leading up to January 6, he was the target of a concerted campaign by Trump and his allies who wanted the Vice President to block or delay or otherwise meddle in the certification of the Electoral College votes by Congress. They wanted them to help them pull off their attempted coup.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the federal judge ordered Pence to testify in the investigation by the special prosecutor \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  . And Pence has indicated he will not appeal that order. But it remains to be seen whether Trump will try and stop him regardless. We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [20:50:00]\par \par \uc2 VELSHI: All right, tonight, in an NBC News exclusive, a nurse who became an unwilling icon of the anti-vaccination movement is finally breaking her silence. It all started at CHI Memorial Hospital in Chattanooga, Tennessee. Back in December 2020, the very first COVID vaccines were being rolled out. And as frontline worker, Nurse Tiffany Dover was one of the first in line. But when she fainted live on 