y through the use of pills rather than surgically. That was true before jobs. And I have to think it`s only more and more so because we know that in places where abortion is banned. This is one way that women are able to help them.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: Here`s what I really don`t get when the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade, Justice Alito`s majority opinion said the issue should go to the states, then how come if this one judge in Amarillo, Texas makes a decision, it could impact all 50 of us.\par \par \uc2 FARHADIAN WEINSTEIN: Exactly. And that`s why this decision is bigger than Dobbs because it can affect all of us. And he said that and the other thing that they said, that the Court said was this is really going to neutralize things and sort of lower the temperature of all the litigation going on around the country. And I think we can say that also did not bear out.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: Yes, that`s true.\par \par \uc2 FARHADIAN WEINSTEIN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: Non of this has been neutralized. Not in the last year. Tali, you always make us smarter. I don`t feel safer, but I feel smarter tonight. Thank you for being here. Fali Farhadian Weinstein.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  dividing the GOP over his Ukraine comments bringing an already there rift in the Republican Party to the surface. Our political panel weighs in when THE 11TH HOUR continues.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [23:33:27]\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. ROGER WICKER (R-MS): I`m very disturbed that that he feels that way. I think clearly we have an interest in Eastern Europe.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOHN THUNE\uc2  (R-SD): I think the majority opinion among Senate Republicans is that the United States has a vital national security interest there and stopping Russian aggression. And that`s certainly the view I have.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  facing blowback from some members of h