. It`s so important for someone to speak to our higher nature, and take on the huge challenges that our faces and not inside issues, these cultural issues that have nothing to do with the prosperity and the future success of our country.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: Well, then why does so many people right, I talked to Republicans are sort of like traditional Republicans all the time. And when I bring up things like January 6, they say like, January 6 was terrible, but it`s in the past.\par \par \uc2 Have you heard that Princeton to Woodrow Wilson`s name off the school? Like, I don`t even understand the false equivalency, right. Culture war issues are over here. Attacks on our democracy should be up here.\par \par \uc2 SHAYS: Well, I have sleepless nights, because I think exactly the way you`re thinking and it`s a Republican Party that`s been captured by someone who spoke for our lower nature and not our higher nature.\par \par \uc2 Think of what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was saying this week, it was all negative, angry stuff, and filled with lots of lies. But one thing that Democrats have to be careful of is they have a very bad record on the issue of immigration. And I know that maybe a lot of your audience wouldn`t agree.\par \par \uc2 But the bottom line is, most Americans want our borders to be protected. And the Democrats are not, on the right side of that, they`re not on the right side of having sanctuary cities, which shows that they don`t really want to address the issue. So you know, it`s the Democrats have problems too.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: Different problems. Juanita, is this a vulnerability for President Biden for the Democratic Party that even when we talk to democratic lawmakers, in border states, especially local ones in border cities, they`re saying we need to do something. Is this a vulnerability for the administration?\par \par \uc2 TOLLIVER: I mean, it`s been a long standing vulnerability for Democrats writ large that Republicans have liked to hit Democrats