ed itself from some of this damaging information coming out. And I think that they believe that the law may prevail in their side, but based on this filing, I find that highly unlikely.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: I want to follow up on that. But just to combine the two points, Howard, what you said about the sort of key pivot here being when they tried to distance themselves a bit from Trump. And Asha, what you`re saying about this not entering the universe is a really amazing moment at CPAC today.\par \par \uc2 Now, the currently under indictment, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  , himself a kind of -- I don`t know what you`d call, you know, two-shirted podcaster want to be media guru. He was up before the crowd and he had an opportunity to tell them about this. Take a listen to what he had to say at CPAC.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 STEVE BANNON\uc2  , FORMER WHITE HOUSE CHIEF STRATEGIST: OK, Murdoch, here`s the way it`s going to be brother. You`ve disrespected \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  long enough. He hasn`t been on Fox News since he announced for presidency.\par \par \uc2 Let me ask you, any guy that brought peace to the world for four years until Chinese led off a bioweapon, right? Wouldn`t you think to have respect for the audience? You would have him back up here to talk about the geopolitical. What if you had respect for people, would do you do that? They don`t respect you, read the depositions, the deposition they have a fear, loathing and contempt for you.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 [20:35:16]\par \par \uc2 HAYES: I should note of course, the Chinese did not detonate a bio weapon. As far as we know, there`s no evidence to support that. So, I just have to note that.\par \par \uc2 They don`t respect you. They have a fear, loathing contempt for you. You know, stop clock right twice a day, Howard. There is something to that as it comes through in those deposition.\par \par \uc2 DEAN: Yes, well, look, Murdoch likes -- cares about two things