gerous because having had access to that footage is going to legitimize whatever he comes out with, not to say that his findings will be legitimate, but he will have the cover of saying well, I have screened all this material. I`ve seen these hours and hours of footage, and I can tell you that this is the case. And that is incredibly dangerous. You know, we`re talking about the video that \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  has access to. This is tied to the January 6 interaction -- insurrection. So, Speaker McCarthy is now providing him with all of it.\par \par \uc2 [23:40:02]\par \par \uc2 This is video that we should remind people that the House panel investigating January 6, the House committee investigating January 6 had to negotiate with the \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  about how to get access to it and sit in the locked room to review it. And now Tucker Carlson is going to have unfettered access to it. Just because January 6 didn`t succeed on January 6, doesn`t mean that that type of thing couldn`t succeed again, in the future. We`re in a very dangerous, precarious time. And it seems to only be getting more divided, more polarized, and more dangerous.\par \par \uc2 You have \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  now calling for a national divorce, which is, you know, a euphemism for a civil war. So, it`s a really, really dangerous time. And at the root of it is what you`re speaking to what we`re seeing happening in Ohio, is just this polarization and this politicization, about everything, even human tragedy.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: But didn`t we think the midterms was a clue to Washington, D.C. that said, America is done with this, let`s get to work. You`re talking about doing the work? And that`s what the midterms asked for. But it`s not what we`re delivering. It`s not what our lawmakers are?\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: No, unfortunately, one thing I`ve learned is that, especially with white people in power, they would rather burn everything down before they would -- I mean, it just is 