 where he can talk like Anita Dunn was saying about what progress has been made. I mean, the bipartisan Safer Communities Act, while it was not the solution to gun violence, it was the first significant legislation to address gun violence in nearly 30 years. And they got it done on a bipartisan basis. It wasn`t a Democratic Party line vote.\par \par \uc2 Here, this is -- this is history being made. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  shaking hands with the new Republican Speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy. Kevin McCarthy has spent his whole life aiming at that chair.\par \par \uc2 [20:35:08]\par \par \uc2 REID: Yes, he does.\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: And he has got himself there.\par \par \uc2 REID: And he should be in miniature because I feel like he is such a tiny speaker in so many ways sort of thematically. He`s physically tall.\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: I mean, we`re going to see him gavel session in here in a moment. There will be a lot of shots like this. These are all live shots of Members of the Senate you`ll see coming in. We`ll soon see Members of the Cabinet. You see the leader of the Republicans in the Senate there on the left side of your screen, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . So, you`ll see a lot of this as we are getting settled in here. Senator Amy Klobuchar, Senator Dick Durbin there behind her.\par \par \uc2 I mean, the thing about McCarthy is that I have to constantly remind myself, Joy, that Kevin McCarthy in this Congress has the same size majority that \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  had in the last Congress.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , despite physical stature, never seemed that small.\par \par \uc2 REID: That`s right.\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: Because she could get her conference to do whatever she wanted whenever she wanted it.\par \par \uc2 REID: That`s right.\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: He is -- he is presiding over something much more.\par \par \uc2 REID: He isn`t \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MADDOW: All right, 