ry around him a little bit because we have -- from most of the major players, there`s some testimony of some kind. \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  never testified before the January 6 Committee but he wrote a book. And more importantly, the people close to him and around him did testify. They`ve testified before a grand jury in Washington and also in the committee. So, we kind of know where \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  was at.\par \par \uc2 Meadows really does feel like this bizarre black hole cipher at the center of the plot. But then when you look at a text like this, and I want to get your reaction to this -- so, this is \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2 . This is him saying on December 30th. If we`re hoping to move real numbers on the sixth, I think we need to quickly start mobilizing our real deal allies. I`m ready to go. I have bodies to help, will follow your lead.\par \par \uc2 Bodies to help is notable there. \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  writes back. Thanks, Jason. You`re the best. I will bring it up with POTUS and I plan to meet with them on Saturday. Like, that`s him furthering it. But again, still this kind of weird cipher.\par \par \uc2 CORN: Yes, well, there`s that, there`s a text that Talking Points Memo revealed from Jim Jordan saying basically, we got to get \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to stop the certification in Congress, and Meadow says I`m working on it. I`m pushing, you know, I`m not sure it`s going to happen. So, he was involved in all this. He was on the phone call to Georgia. He refuses to discuss anything on his book. He refuses to talk about it publicly. He`s trying to get out of testifying in Georgia, right? He hasn`t testified to the January 6th Committee. He was up to his neck in all the various coup attempts.\par \par \uc2 [20:25:00]\par \par \uc2 And you`re right, he`s a bit of a black hole. Maybe when the January 6 Committee puts out its final report in the next week or so, we`ll have more details if they haven`t yet shared with us.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: It`s one of the things 